Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:04.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}We present DS-1000,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.68,0:00:08.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a natural and reliable benchmark for data science code generation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.86,0:00:12.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}DS-1000 gathers a thousand real problems across seven widely used Python libraries such as NumPy and Pandas,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.04,0:00:17.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}all drawn from StackOverflow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.22,0:00:21.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It pairs these realistic problems with reliable execution-based evaluation and a built-in
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.40,0:00:25.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}defense against memorization,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.58,0:00:29.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}giving the community a trustworthy yardstick for data science coding models.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.06,0:00:32.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Data science coding is central to many fields,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.04,0:00:38.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}yet it demands fluency in specialized libraries that create real barriers for everyday users.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.06,0:00:42.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Code generation models could lower those barriers,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.30,0:00:46.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but the community lacked a benchmark to measure real progress.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.32,0:00:52.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Most existing datasets focus on competitive or interview-style problems that test algorithms
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.28,0:00:54.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}rather than real-world usage,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.16,0:01:01.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and many score answers with surface-form metrics like BLEU that drift away from what programmers actually intend.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.48,0:01:06.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}There was no benchmark combining natural, richly contextual problems with a reliable,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.98,0:01:09.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}execution-based way to judge correctness.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.94,0:01:14.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Real data science questions rarely look like clean textbook prompts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.61,0:01:19.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On StackOverflow, users describe messy contexts: their broken code,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.20,0:01:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the error they hit, and concrete input-output examples of what they want.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.21,0:01:27.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Prior benchmarks strip that richness away.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.09,0:01:29.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}At the same time, as models get better,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.77,0:01:32.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}surface-form scores like BLEU become misleading,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.06,0:01:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}rewarding text that looks right but does not run.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.42,0:01:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This motivates a benchmark built from natural problems and judged by actually executing the code.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.38,0:01:47.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}DS-1000 makes three contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.42,0:01:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First, it provides a thousand realistic problems with diverse contexts,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.46,0:01:55.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}adapted from naturally occurring StackOverflow questions across seven popular Python libraries.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.51,0:01:59.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.55,0:02:03.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it implements reliable multi-criteria evaluation that runs test cases and checks surface-form constraints,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.59,0:02:07.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so accepted solutions are almost always genuinely correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.63,0:02:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.67,0:02:15.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it proactively defends against memorization by perturbing problems so models cannot simply
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.72,0:02:19.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}recall pre-training answers.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.76,0:02:23.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors release the benchmark and use it to evaluate five state-of-the-art code models.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.10,0:02:27.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}DS-1000 is built through a five-stage pipeline.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.21,0:02:30.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Annotators first select high-vote, testable, useful,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.65,0:02:35.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and representative StackOverflow problems and rewrite them for clarity.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.35,0:02:41.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}They add a code context with insertion markers showing exactly where the model must fill in code.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.77,0:02:47.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}They then implement automatic tests that check functional correctness by executing test
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.53,0:02:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}cases and also enforce surface-form constraints,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.71,0:02:54.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}such as forbidding certain APIs or keywords in the syntax tree.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.88,0:02:59.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To defend against memorization, they perturb each original problem,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.31,0:03:06.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}using surface perturbations that leave the reference solution unchanged and semantic perturbations that change it,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.86,0:03:09.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}plus deliberately difficult rewrites.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.31,0:03:14.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Finally they red-team the evaluation, requiring it to reject known-wrong solutions.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.80,0:03:20.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Every problem, solution, and metric is reviewed by at least three expert annotators.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.66,0:03:27.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}DS-1000 contains a thousand problems originating from four hundred fifty-one unique StackOverflow posts,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.77,0:03:33.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}spanning seven widely used Python libraries: NumPy, Pandas, TensorFlow, PyTorch,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.24,0:03:35.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}SciPy, Scikit-learn, and Matplotlib.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.70,0:03:41.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}More than half of the problems are modified from their sources to resist memorization,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.58,0:03:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}including one hundred fifty-two surface perturbations,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.27,0:03:48.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}two hundred thirty-five semantic perturbations,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.48,0:03:51.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and one hundred sixty-two difficult rewrites.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.56,0:03:56.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On average each problem has one point six test cases, one hundred forty words,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.89,0:04:00.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a reference solution of three point six lines,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.31,0:04:03.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and about one in five carry surface-form constraints.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.93,0:04:07.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}With a hundred forty average words per problem,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.15,0:04:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}DS-1000 is far richer in context than other data science datasets.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.96,0:04:15.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}DS-1000 clearly separates models of different strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.86,0:04:19.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The best public system, Codex-002 in the insertion format,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.97,0:04:24.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reaches only forty-three point three percent average accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.37,0:04:29.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}nontrivial but far from solved, leaving substantial room for improvement.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.54,0:04:32.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Across five models from three families,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.30,0:04:38.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}accuracy ranges from seven point four percent up to forty-three point three percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.26,0:04:41.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Insertion format, which supplies right-hand context,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.94,0:04:46.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}gives Codex-002 a four point one percent boost over completion format,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.91,0:04:51.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}underscoring the value of infilling for data science coding.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.16,0:04:57.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Weaker models such as CodeGen-6B and InCoder-6B fall below five percent on some libraries.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.84,0:04:59.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To show why memorization matters,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.06,0:05:03.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the authors probe the popular numpy-100 problem set.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.55,0:05:07.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Codex-002 scores seventy-two point five percent there,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.17,0:05:11.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but accuracy collapses to forty point six percent after perturbation,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.80,0:05:17.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and in thirty-six percent of semantic cases the model still returns the original,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.24,0:05:18.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}now-incorrect answer,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.65,0:05:23.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}evidence that it is recalling memorized solutions rather than reasoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.48,0:05:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On DS-1000 the perturbation drop is much gentler, about three to nine percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.72,0:05:31.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}because these problems appear less often online.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.94,0:05:37.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This confirms perturbation as a practical defense against memorization by future models.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.15,0:05:40.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A few numbers capture DS-1000.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.23,0:05:43.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It offers a thousand problems over seven libraries,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.77,0:05:47.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}drawn from four hundred fifty-one unique StackOverflow posts.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.00,0:05:52.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The best model reaches only forty-three point three percent accuracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.79,0:05:57.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The evaluation is highly reliable: among all solutions it accepts,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.36,0:06:00.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}just one point eight percent are actually incorrect,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.97,0:06:05.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and only about half a percent of rejected ones are truly correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.48,0:06:09.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And with a hundred forty words per problem on average,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.22,0:06:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}its contexts are far richer than comparable datasets.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.20,0:06:18.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}DS-1000 gives the community a data science code benchmark that is realistic,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.08,0:06:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reliably evaluated, and resistant to memorization.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.29,0:06:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Because it is built from natural StackOverflow problems,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.88,0:06:29.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}judged by executing code against test cases and surface-form constraints,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.57,0:06:34.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and defended by deliberate perturbation, its scores are trustworthy and hard to game.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.02,0:06:40.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And because even the strongest model reaches only forty-three point three percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.29,0:06:45.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it makes clear how much room remains for progress in data science code generation.
